></rect><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"16\" y1=\"6\" y2=\"6\"></line><line x1=\"16\" x2=\"16\" y1=\"14\" y2=\"18\"></line><path d=\"M16 10h.01\"></path><path d=\"M12 10h.01\"></path><path d=\"M8 10h.01\"></path><path d=\"M12 14h.01\"></path><path d=\"M8 14h.01\"></path><path d=\"M12 18h.01\"></path><path d=\"M8 18h.01\"></path></svg>Calculators<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-3 w-3 transition-transform\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></button></div><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/compare\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg>Compare</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/glossary\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-book-open h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 7v14\"></path><path d=\"M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z\"></path></svg>Glossary</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/blog\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-book-open h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 7v14\"></path><path d=\"M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z\"></path></svg>Blog</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/salary\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-trending-up h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 7h6v6\"></path><path d=\"m22 7-8.5 8.5-5-5L2 17\"></path></svg>Salary</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/tax-data\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Data</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/widgets\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg>Widgets</a></nav><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><a class=\"hidden sm:flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Calculate Now</a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:bg-accent dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 rounded-md gap-1.5 px-3 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 lg:hidden text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground\" aria-label=\"Toggle mobile menu\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 18h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 6h16\"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id=\"main-content\" class=\"flex-1\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/salary-comparison-calculator#software\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"Salary Comparison Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/salary-comparison-calculator\",\"applicationCategory\":\"FinanceApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Web\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":0,\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"availability\":\"https://schema.org/InStock\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/salary-comparison-calculator\"},\"description\":\"Compare salaries after federal, state, and FICA taxes side by side for all 50 states. Free 2026 calculator.\",\"provider\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#organization\"},\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Rachel Mitchell\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"jobTitle\":\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director, CPA\",\"description\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\",\"knowsAbout\":[\"Federal Income Tax\",\"State Income Tax\",\"FICA Tax\",\"Payroll Tax\",\"IRS Compliance\",\"Tax Planning\",\"Multi-State Taxation\",\"Tax-Advantaged Accounts\"],\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachelmitchellcpa/\",\"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/\"],\"worksFor\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"image\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/salary-comparison-calculator#faq\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I compare salaries in different states?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Enter each salary and select the corresponding state. The calculator will show you the after-tax take-home pay for each scenario side by side, including federal tax, FICA (Social Security and Medicare), and state income tax. The difference column highlights exactly how much more or less you would take home.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Why is the after-tax difference bigger than the salary difference?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"State income tax rates vary dramatically — from 0% in Texas, Florida, and Washington to over 13% in California. A $10,000 salary increase in California might result in only $6,000 more after taxes, while the same $10,000 increase in Texas gives you nearly $7,700 more. This calculator shows you the real, after-tax value of any salary difference.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does this include FICA taxes (Social Security and Medicare)?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Every scenario includes the full 6.2% Social Security tax (up to the 2026 wage base of $184,500) and 1.45% Medicare tax, plus the 0.9% Additional Medicare Tax for incomes over $200,000. These are the same regardless of state, but they reduce your take-home pay significantly.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I compare job offers with different benefits?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. You can adjust 401(k) contributions and HSA contributions for each scenario. If one job offers a 5% 401(k) match and another does not, enter the contribution amounts to see how pre-tax deductions affect your net take-home pay.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is this calculator accurate for 2026?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. All federal tax brackets, standard deductions, FICA rates, and state tax rates are updated for the 2026 tax year. The 2026 Social Security wage base is $184,500, the standard deduction is $16,100 for single filers, and state rates reflect the latest published figures from each state revenue department.\"}}]},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/salary-comparison-calculator#breadcrumb\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Salary Comparison Calculator\"}]}]}</script><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><a class=\"underline underline-offset-2 decoration-muted-foreground/40 hover:decoration-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors flex items-center gap-1\" href=\"/\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-house h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M15 21v-8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8\"></path><path d=\"M3 10a2 2 0 0 1 .709-1.528l7-5.999a2 2 0 0 1 2.582 0l7 5.999A2 2 0 0 1 21 10v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z\"></path></svg><span class=\"hidden sm:inline\">Home</span></a><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5 text-muted-foreground\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg><span class=\"text-foreground font-medium\">Salary Comparison Calculator</span></span></nav><div class=\"mb-10 text-center\"><div class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 border border-blue-500/20 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-blue-400 mb-6\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg>Side-by-Side Comparison</div><h1 class=\"text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-5xl\">Salary Comparison<!-- --> <span class=\"gradient-text\">Calculator</span></h1><p class=\"mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Compare after-tax salaries across different states, filing statuses, and deduction levels. See which salary actually puts more money in your pocket.</p></div><section class=\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6 text-center\">How It <span class=\"gradient-text\">Works</span></h2><div class=\"grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3\"><div class=\"text-center\"><div class=\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\">1</div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\">Enter Each Salary</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Input up to 4 salaries with their states and filing statuses.</p></div><div class=\"text-center\"><div class=\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\">2</div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\">See After-Tax Results</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The calculator shows net take-home pay for each scenario side by side.</p></div><div class=\"text-center\"><div class=\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\">3</div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\">Compare &amp; Decide</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The difference column reveals which salary gives you more after-tax income.</p></div></div></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><div id=\"scenario-comparison\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><div data-state=\"closed\" data-slot=\"collapsible\"><div data-slot=\"card\" class=\"text-card-foreground flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-xl border py-6 shadow-sm border-blue-500/20 bg-card/80 backdrop-blur-sm\"><div data-slot=\"collapsible-trigger\" class=\"@container/card-header grid auto-rows-min grid-rows-[auto_auto] items-start gap-1.5 px-6 has-data-[slot=card-action]:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] [.border-b]:pb-6 cursor-pointer pb-4 transition-colors hover:bg-muted/30\" type=\"button\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_5av5uhtb_\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-state=\"closed\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-5 w-5 text-blue-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg><div data-slot=\"card-title\" class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">Compare Tax Scenarios</div><span data-slot=\"badge\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border px-2 py-0.5 font-medium w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden [a&amp;]:hover:bg-accent [a&amp;]:hover:text-accent-foreground text-xs border-blue-500/30 text-blue-400\">New</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground transition-transform\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></div><div data-slot=\"card-description\" class=\"text-muted-foreground text-sm\">Compare up to 4 scenarios side by side — different states, 401(k) contributions, or filing statuses</div></div><div data-state=\"closed\" id=\"radix-_R_5av5uhtb_\" hidden=\"\" data-slot=\"collapsible-content\"></div></div></div></div></section><section class=\"mb-10 space-y-6\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\">Why After-Tax Salary <span class=\"gradient-text\">Comparison Matters</span></h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">A $100,000 salary in California is not the same as a $100,000 salary in Texas — not even close. After federal taxes, FICA deductions, and state income tax, the Texas earner takes home roughly $7,000 to $10,000 more per year. When you are evaluating job offers, negotiating a raise, or considering relocation, the gross salary number alone is misleading. You need to see the after-tax, take-home pay to make an informed decision. Our salary comparison calculator shows you exactly what each salary means in real dollars, accounting for the 2026 federal tax brackets, the Social Security wage base of $184,500, Medicare taxes, and state-specific income tax rates for all 50 states.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10 space-y-6\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\">When to Use a <span class=\"gradient-text\">Salary Comparison Calculator</span></h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">There are five common situations where comparing after-tax salaries is essential for making a smart financial decision. First, when you receive a job offer in a different state — a $120,000 offer in California may actually pay less than a $110,000 offer in Texas after state income tax. Second, when your employer offers remote work — you may be able to relocate to a no-income-tax state without changing jobs. Third, when comparing two job offers with different base salaries, bonus structures, or benefit packages. Fourth, when planning a relocation for personal reasons (family, lifestyle) and you need to know if your salary will stretch far enough. Fifth, when negotiating a raise — knowing your effective tax rate helps you calculate the after-tax value of any salary increase.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">A common mistake is comparing gross salaries without accounting for state taxes. A $100,000 offer in Texas yields about $79,180 in take-home pay, while the same $100,000 in California yields about $73,799 — a difference of $5,381 per year, or about $448 per month. Over a five-year period, that&#x27;s nearly $27,000 in lost take-home pay. Our salary comparison calculator makes these differences immediately visible, so you can negotiate or decide with full information.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\">Real-World <span class=\"gradient-text\">Salary Comparisons</span></h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground mb-4\">Here&#x27;s how the same salary translates to different take-home pay depending on which state you live in. These are real numbers from our 2026 tax calculations:</p><div class=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border/30 mb-4\"><table class=\"w-full text-sm\"><thead class=\"bg-muted/30\"><tr><th class=\"text-left p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\">Salary</th><th class=\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\">No-Tax State</th><th class=\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\">Take-Home</th><th class=\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\">High-Tax State</th><th class=\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\">Take-Home</th><th class=\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\">Difference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"border-t border-border/20\"><td class=\"p-3 font-medium text-foreground\">$75,000</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\">Texas<!-- --> (<!-- -->TX<!-- -->)</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-medium\">$61,593</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\">California<!-- --> (<!-- -->CA<!-- -->)</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-foreground\">$58,536</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-bold\">+<!-- -->$3,056</td></tr><tr class=\"border-t border-border/20\"><td class=\"p-3 font-medium text-foreground\">$100,000</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\">Florida<!-- --> (<!-- -->FL<!-- -->)</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-medium\">$79,180</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\">New York<!-- --> (<!-- -->NY<!-- -->)</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-foreground\">$74,234</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-bold\">+<!-- -->$4,946</td></tr><tr class=\"border-t border-border/20\"><td class=\"p-3 font-medium text-foreground\">$150,000</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\">Washington<!-- --> (<!-- -->WA<!-- -->)</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-medium\">$113,791</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\">California<!-- --> (<!-- -->CA<!-- -->)</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-foreground\">$103,760</td><td class=\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-bold\">+<!-- -->$10,031</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">* Calculations assume single filing status, 2026 standard deduction of $16,100, and no pre-tax contributions. NYC residents would pay additional city tax not shown here.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10 space-y-4\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\">Factors That <span class=\"gradient-text\">Affect Salary Comparison</span></h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Beyond state income tax, several other factors influence the real take-home pay difference between two salaries:</p><ul class=\"space-y-3 text-muted-foreground\"><li class=\"flex gap-3\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">1</span><span><strong class=\"text-foreground\">Filing status</strong> — Married filing jointly doubles the standard deduction to $32,200 and uses wider tax brackets, reducing federal tax significantly compared to single filing status.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">2</span><span><strong class=\"text-foreground\">401(k) contributions</strong> — Pre-tax contributions reduce your federal and state taxable income. A $10,000 401(k) contribution at the 22% marginal rate saves you $2,200 in federal tax plus state tax savings.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">3</span><span><strong class=\"text-foreground\">HSA contributions</strong> — Triple-tax-advantaged. Reduces FICA, federal, and state taxable income. The 2026 limit is $4,400 (self) or $8,300 (family).</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">4</span><span><strong class=\"text-foreground\">NYC residency</strong> — If you live in NYC, add 3.078%–3.876% city tax on top of New York state tax. This can reduce a $100K salary&#x27;s take-home by another $3,500+ per year.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">5</span><span><strong class=\"text-foreground\">Additional Medicare Tax</strong> — Above $200,000 (single), add 0.9% Medicare surtax. This affects high earners and isn&#x27;t matched by employers.</span></li></ul></section><section class=\"mb-10 space-y-4\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\">Common <span class=\"gradient-text\">Mistakes</span> When Comparing Salaries</h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">When evaluating job offers or planning a relocation, watch out for these common pitfalls:</p><div class=\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\"><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-rose-500/20 bg-rose-500/5 p-4\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2 text-sm\">❌ Comparing Gross Salaries Only</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">A $120K offer in CA vs $110K in TX — the TX offer may actually pay more after taxes. Always compare take-home, not gross.</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-rose-500/20 bg-rose-500/5 p-4\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2 text-sm\">❌ Forgetting Property Tax</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Texas has 1.71% property tax vs California&#x27;s 0.71%. On a $500K home, that&#x27;s $5,000/year extra in TX.</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-rose-500/20 bg-rose-500/5 p-4\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2 text-sm\">❌ Ignoring 401(k) Match</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">A 5% match on $100K is $5,000 of &quot;free&quot; pre-tax money. Include this in your total compensation comparison.</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-rose-500/20 bg-rose-500/5 p-4\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2 text-sm\">❌ Overlooking Cost of Living</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">$100K in San Francisco is barely middle class; $100K in Houston is comfortable. Adjust for local costs.</p></div></div></section><section class=\"mb-10 space-y-4\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\">How to <span class=\"gradient-text\">Use Your Results</span></h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Once you&#x27;ve compared after-tax salaries, the next step is to factor in cost-of-living differences. A $5,000/year take-home advantage in Texas could be erased if housing costs $500 more per month. Use our <a class=\"text-emerald-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/relocation-calculator\">Relocation Calculator</a> <!-- -->to factor in housing, utilities, transportation, and groceries for a complete picture.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">For job offer comparisons, don&#x27;t forget to include equity, bonuses, and benefits. A lower base salary with a 20% bonus target and stock options may outperform a higher base salary with no upside. Our <a class=\"text-emerald-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/job-offer-comparison-calculator\">Job Offer Comparison Calculator</a> <!-- -->handles these more complex scenarios.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Finally, remember that tax brackets and rates change annually. The 2026 numbers in this calculator reflect the latest IRS and state revenue department figures, but always verify with a tax professional before making major financial decisions.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\">Salary Comparison <span class=\"gradient-text\">FAQ</span></h2><div class=\"space-y-3\"><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">How do I compare salaries in different states?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Enter each salary and select the corresponding state. The calculator will show you the after-tax take-home pay for each scenario side by side, including federal tax, FICA (Social Security and Medicare), and state income tax. The difference column highlights exactly how much more or less you would take home.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Why is the after-tax difference bigger than the salary difference?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">State income tax rates vary dramatically — from 0% in Texas, Florida, and Washington to over 13% in California. A $10,000 salary increase in California might result in only $6,000 more after taxes, while the same $10,000 increase in Texas gives you nearly $7,700 more. This calculator shows you the real, after-tax value of any salary difference.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Does this include FICA taxes (Social Security and Medicare)?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Yes. Every scenario includes the full 6.2% Social Security tax (up to the 2026 wage base of $184,500) and 1.45% Medicare tax, plus the 0.9% Additional Medicare Tax for incomes over $200,000. These are the same regardless of state, but they reduce your take-home pay significantly.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Can I compare job offers with different benefits?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Yes. You can adjust 401(k) contributions and HSA contributions for each scenario. If one job offers a 5% 401(k) match and another does not, enter the contribution amounts to see how pre-tax deductions affect your net take-home pay.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Is this calculator accurate for 2026?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Yes. All federal tax brackets, standard deductions, FICA rates, and state tax rates are updated for the 2026 tax year. The 2026 Social Security wage base is $184,500, the standard deduction is $16,100 for single filers, and state rates reflect the latest published figures from each state revenue department.</div></details></div></section><section class=\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-8 text-center\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Related Calculators</h2><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\">Paycheck Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/job-offer-comparison-calculator\">Job Offer Comparison</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/paycheck-difference-calculator\">Paycheck Difference</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/compare\">Compare State Taxes</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/salary\">Salary After Tax</a></div></section><section class=\"py-12 border-t border-border/20\"><section aria-label=\"Author: Rachel Mitchell\" class=\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500/5 to-card/80 p-5 sm:p-6\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-4\"><img src=\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\" alt=\"Rachel Mitchell, CPA\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\" class=\"h-12 w-12 shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover ring-1 ring-emerald-500/30\" loading=\"lazy\"/><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2\"><a class=\"text-base font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors\" href=\"/about#rachel-mitchell\">Rachel Mitchell</a><span class=\"inline-flex items-center rounded-md bg-emerald-500/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-400 ring-1 ring-emerald-500/25\">CPA</span></div><p class=\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Lead Tax Analyst &amp; Editorial Director<!-- -->, TheTaxCalc</p><p class=\"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground line-clamp-2\">Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.</p><div class=\"mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1\"><svg class=\"h-3 w-3 text-emerald-500/60\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M6.75 3v2.25M17.25 3v2.25M3 18.75V7.5a2.25 2.25 0 012.25-2.25h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 7.5v11.25m-18 0A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75m-18 0v-7.5A2.25 2.25 0 015.25 9h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 11.25v7.5\"></path></svg>Reviewed: January 2026</span><span>Tax data verified against IRS Publication 15-T &amp; state revenue departments</span></div></div></div></section></section></div><!--$--><!--/$--></main><footer class=\"mt-auto border-t border-border/30 glass-strong\"><div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-500/5 via-emerald-500/10 to-emerald-500/5 border-b border-border/20\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><div class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:justify-between\"><div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-foreground\">Stay Updated on <span class=\"text-emerald-400\">Tax Changes</span></h2><p class=\"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Get the latest tax tips, calculator updates, and financial insights delivered to your inbox.</p></div><div class=\"flex w-full max-w-sm gap-2\"><input type=\"email\" data-slot=\"input\" class=\"file:text-foreground selection:bg-primary selection:text-primary-foreground dark:bg-input/30 flex h-9 w-full min-w-0 rounded-md border px-3 py-1 text-base shadow-xs transition-[co