fferent states, filing statuses, and deduction levels. See which salary actually puts more money in your pocket.\\\"}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"25:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6 text-center\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"How It \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"gradient-text\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Works\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-center\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"1\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Enter Each Salary\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Input up to 4 salaries with their states and filing statuses.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-center\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"2\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"See After-Tax Results\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The calculator shows net take-home pay for each scenario side by side.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-center\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"3\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Compare \\u0026 Decide\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The difference column reveals which salary gives you more after-tax income.\\\"}]]}]]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"26:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-10\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L38\\\",null,{\\\"defaultScenario\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"default\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Current Salary\\\",\\\"salary\\\":75000,\\\"payFrequency\\\":\\\"annual\\\",\\\"stateKey\\\":\\\"illinois\\\",\\\"filingStatus\\\":\\\"single\\\",\\\"retirement401k\\\":0,\\\"hsaContribution\\\":0,\\\"nycResident\\\":false}}]}]\\n27:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-10 space-y-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Why After-Tax Salary \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"gradient-text\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Comparison Matters\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"A $100,000 salary in California is not the same as a $100,000 salary in Texas — not even close. After federal taxes, FICA deductions, and state income tax, the Texas earner takes home roughly $7,000 to $10,000 more per year. When you are evaluating job offers, negotiating a raise, or considering relocation, the gross salary number alone is misleading. You need to see the after-tax, take-home pay to make an informed decision. Our salary comparison calculator shows you exactly what each salary means in real dollars, accounting for the 2026 federal tax brackets, the Social Security wage base of $184,500, Medicare taxes, and state-specific income tax rates for all 50 states.\\\"}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"28:[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-10 space-y-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"When to Use a \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"gradient-text\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Salary Comparison Calculator\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"There are five common situations where comparing after-tax salaries is essential for making a smart financial decision. First, when you receive a job offer in a different state — a $120,000 offer in California may actually pay less than a $110,000 offer in Texas after state income tax. Second, when your employer offers remote work — you may be able to relocate to a no-income-tax state without changing jobs. Third, when comparing two job offers with different base salaries, bonus structures, or benefit packages. Fourth, when planning a relocation for personal reasons (family, lifestyle) and you need to know if your salary will stretch far enough. Fifth, when negotiating a raise — knowing your effective tax rate helps you calculate the after-tax value of any salary increase.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"A common mistake is comparing gross salaries without accounting for state taxes. A $100,000 offer in Texas yields about $79,180 in take-home pay, while the same $100,000 in California yields about $73,799 — a difference of $5,381 per year, or about $448 per month. Over a five-year period, that's nearly $27,000 in lost take-home pay. Our salary comparison calculator makes these differences immediately visible, so you can negotiate or decide with full information.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-10\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Real-World \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"gradient-text\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Salary Comparisons\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Here's how the same salary translates to different take-home pay depending on which state you live in. These are real numbers from our 2026 tax calculations:\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border/30 mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"table\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"w-full text-sm\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"thead\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-muted/30\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tr\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-left p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Salary\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"No-Tax State\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Take-Home\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"High-Tax State\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Take-Home\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Difference\\\"}]]}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tbody\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tr\\\",\\\"75000\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"border-t border-border/20\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",