\"h9nckh\",{\"d\":\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"g4d7ey\",{\"d\":\"M4 17h16\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],\"Side-by-Side Comparison\"]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-5xl\",\"children\":[\"Salary Comparison\",\" \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"Calculator\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Compare after-tax salaries across different states, filing statuses, and deduction levels. See which salary actually puts more money in your pocket.\"}]]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6 text-center\",\"children\":[\"How It \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"Works\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\",\"children\":\"1\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\",\"children\":\"Enter Each Salary\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Input up to 4 salaries with their states and filing statuses.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\",\"children\":\"2\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\",\"children\":\"See After-Tax Results\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The calculator shows net take-home pay for each scenario side by side.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\",\"children\":\"3\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\",\"children\":\"Compare & Decide\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The difference column reveals which salary gives you more after-tax income.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L38\",null,{\"defaultScenario\":{\"id\":\"default\",\"label\":\"Current Salary\",\"salary\":75000,\"payFrequency\":\"annual\",\"stateKey\":\"illinois\",\"filingStatus\":\"single\",\"retirement401k\":0,\"hsaContribution\":0,\"nycResident\":false}}]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 space-y-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Why After-Tax Salary \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"Comparison Matters\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"A $100,000 salary in California is not the same as a $100,000 salary in Texas — not even close. After federal taxes, FICA deductions, and state income tax, the Texas earner takes home roughly $7,000 to $10,000 more per year. When you are evaluating job offers, negotiating a raise, or considering relocation, the gross salary number alone is misleading. You need to see the after-tax, take-home pay to make an informed decision. Our salary comparison calculator shows you exactly what each salary means in real dollars, accounting for the 2026 federal tax brackets, the Social Security wage base of $184,500, Medicare taxes, and state-specific income tax rates for all 50 states.\"}]]}]\n28:[[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 space-y-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\",\"children\":[\"When to Use a \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"Salary Comparison Calculator\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"There are five common situations where comparing after-tax salaries is essential for making a smart financial decision. First, when you receive a job offer in a different state — a $120,000 offer in California may actually pay less than a $110,000 offer in Texas after state income tax. Second, when your employer offers remote work — you may be able to relocate to a no-income-tax state without changing jobs. Third, when comparing two job offers with different base salaries, bonus structures, or benefit packages. Fourth, when planning a relocation for personal reasons (family, lifestyle) and you need to know if your salary will stretch far enough. Fifth, when negotiating a raise — knowing your effective tax rate helps you calculate the after-tax value of any salary increase.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"A common mistake is comparing gross salaries without accounting for state taxes. A $100,000 offer in Texas yields about $79,180 in take-home pay, while the same $100,000 in California yields about $73,799 — a difference of $5,381 per year, or about $448 per month. Over a five-year period, that's nearly $27,000 in lost take-home pay. Our salary comparison calculator makes these differences immediately visible, so you can negotiate or decide with full information.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\",\"children\":[\"Real-World \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"Salary Comparisons\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Here's how the same salary translates to different take-home pay depending on which state you live in. These are real numbers from our 2026 tax calculations:\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border/30 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted/30\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-left p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Salary\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"No-Tax State\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Take-Home\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"High-Tax State\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Take-Home\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-right p-3 font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Difference\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"tbody\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",\"75000\",{\"className\":\"border-t border-border/20\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$75,000\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Texas\",\" (\",\"TX\",\")\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-medium\",\"children\":\"$$61,593\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"California\",\" (\",\"CA\",\")\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$58,536\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-bold\",\"children\":[\"+\",\"$$3,056\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"100000\",{\"className\":\"border-t border-border/20\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$100,000\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Florida\",\" (\",\"FL\",\")\"]}],\"$L39\",\"$L3a\",\"$L3b\",\"$L3c\"]}],\"$L3d\"]}]]}]}],\"$L3e\"]}],\"$L3f\",\"$L40\",\"$L41\"]\n29:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\",\"children\":[\"Salary Comparison \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm sm:text-base\",\"children\":\"How do I compare salaries in different states?\"}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"qrunsl\",{\"d\":\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Enter each salary and select the corresponding state. The calculator will show you the after-tax take-home pay for each scenario side by side, including federal tax, FICA (Social Security and Medicare), and state income tax. The difference column highlights exactly how much more or less you would take home.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm sm:text-base\",\"children\":\"Why is the after-tax difference bigger than the salary difference?\"}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"qrunsl\",{\"d\":\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"State income tax rates vary dramatically — from 0% in Texas, Florida, and Washington to over 13% in California. A $10,000 salary increase in California might result in only $6,000 more after taxes, while the same $10,000 increase in Texas gives you nearly $7,700 more. This calculator shows you the real, after-tax value of any salary difference.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm sm:text-base\",\"children\":\"Does this include FICA taxes (Social Security and Medicare)?\"}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"qrunsl\",{\"d\":\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes. Every scenario includes the full 6.2% Social Security tax (up to the 2026 wage base of $184,500) and 1.45% Medicare tax, plus the 0.9% Additional Medicare Tax for incomes over $200,000. These are the same regardless of state, but they reduce your take-home pay significantly.\"}]]}],\"$L42\",\"$L43\"]}]]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-8 text-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Related Calculators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L13\",\"/paycheck-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/paycheck-calculator\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\",\"children\":\"Paycheck Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"$L13\",\"/job-offer-comparison-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/job-offer-comparison-calculator\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\",\"children\":\"Job Offer Comparison\"}],[\"$\",\"$L13\",\"/paycheck-difference-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/paycheck-difference-calculator\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\",\"children\":\"Paycheck Difference\"}],[\"$\",\"$L13\",\"/compare\",{\"href\":\"/compare\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\",\"children\":\"Compare State Taxes\"}],[\"$\",\"$L13\",\"/salary\",{\"href\":\"/salary\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\",\"children\":\"Salary After Tax\"}]]}]]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"py-12 border-t border-border/20\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Author: Rachel Mitchell\",\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500/5 to-card/80 p-5 sm:p-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\",\"alt\":\"Rachel Mitchell, CPA\",\"width\":48,\"height\":48,\"className\":\"h-12 w-12 shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover ring-1 ring-emerald-500/30\",\"loading\":\"lazy\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0 flex-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L13\",null,{\"href\":\"/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"className\":\"text-base font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Rachel Mitchell\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-md bg-emerald-500/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-400 ring-1 ring-emerald-500/25\",\"children\":\"CPA\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director\",\", TheTaxCalc\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-3 w-3 text-emerald-500/60\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M6.75 3v2.25M17.25 3v2.25M3 18.75V7.5a2.25 2.25 0 012.25-2.25h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 7.5v11.25m-18 0A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75m-18 0v-7.5A2.25 2.25 0 015.25 9h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 11.25v7.5\"}]}],\"Reviewed: January 2026\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Tax data verified against IRS Publication 15-T & state revenue departments\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/41ushzejcf42p.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-1\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/1glrjuo8umpnl.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-2\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/3i1397gj6cynn.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-3\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/1l83f0l5jzis_.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n30:[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$35\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@45\"}]}]\n39:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-medium\",\"children\":\"$$79,180\"}]\n3a:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"New York\",\" (\",\"NY\",\")\"]}]\n3b:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$74,234\"}]\n3c:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-bold\",\"children\":[\"+\",\"$$4,946\"]}]\n3d:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"150000\",{\"className\":\"border-t border-border/20\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$150,000\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Washington\",\" (\",\"WA\",\")\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-medium\",\"children\":\"$$113,791\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"California\",\" (\",\"CA\",\")\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$103,760\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 text-right text-emerald-400 font-bold\",\"children\":[\"+\",\"$$10,031\"]}]]}]\n3e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"* Calculations assume single filing status, 2026 standard deduction of $16,100, and no pre-tax contributions. NYC residents would pay additional city tax not shown here.\"}]\n3f:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Factors That \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"Affect Salary Comparison\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Beyond state income tax, several other factors influence the real take-home pay difference between two salaries:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"1\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Filing status\"}],\" — Married filing jointly doubles the standard deduction to $32,200 and uses wider tax brackets, reducing federal tax significantly compared to single filing status.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"2\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"401(k) contributions\"}],\" — Pre-tax contributions reduce your federal and state taxable income. A $10,000 401(k) contribution at the 22% marginal rate saves you $2,200 in federal tax plus state tax savings.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"3\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"HSA contributions\"}],\" — Triple-tax-advantaged. Reduces FICA, federal, and state taxable income. The 2026 limit is $4,400 (self) or $8,300 (family).\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"4\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"NYC residency\"}],\" — If you live in NYC, add 3.078%–3.876% city tax on top of New York state tax. This can reduce a $100K salary's take-home by another $3,500+ per year.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"5\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Additional Medicare Tax\"}],\" — Above $200,000 (single), add 0.9% Medicare surtax. This affects high earners and isn't matched by employers.\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n40:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Common \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"Mistakes\"}],\" When Comparing Salaries\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"When evaluating job offers or planning a relocation, watch out for these common pitfalls:\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-rose-500/20 bg-rose-500/5 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2 text-sm\",\"children\":\"❌ Comparing Gross Salaries Only\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"A $120K offer in CA vs $110K in TX — the TX offer may actually pay more after taxes. Always compare take-home, not gross.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-rose-500/20 bg-rose-500/5 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2 text-sm\",\"children\":\"❌ Forgetting Property Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Texas has 1.71% property tax vs California's 0.71%. On a $500K home, that's $5,000/year extra in TX.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-rose-500/20 bg-rose-500/5 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2 text-sm\",\"children\":\"❌ Ignoring 401(k) Match\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"A 5% match on $100K is $5,000 of \\\"free\\\" pre-tax money. Include this in your total compensation comparison.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-rose-500/20 bg-rose-500/5 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2 text-sm\",\"children\":\"❌ Overlooking Cost of Living\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"$$100K in San Francisco is barely middle class; $100K in Houston is comfortable. Adjust for local costs.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n41:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\",\"children\":[\"How to \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"gradient-text\",\"children\":\"Use Your Results\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"Once you've compared after-tax salaries, the next step is to factor in cost-of-living differences. A $5,000/year take-home advantage in Texas could be erased if housing costs $500 more per month. Use our \",[\"$\",\"$L13\",null,{\"href\":\"/relocation-calculator\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Relocation Calculator\"}],\" \",\"to factor in housing, utilities, transportation, and groceries for a complete picture.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"For job offer comparisons, don't forget to include equity, bonuses, and benefits. A lower base salary with a 20% bonus target and stock options may outperform a higher base salary with no upside. Our \",[\"$\",\"$L13\",null,{\"href\":\"/job-offer-comparison-calculator\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Job Offer Comparison Calculator\"}],\" \",\"handles these more complex scenarios.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Finally, remember that tax brackets and rates change annually. The 2026 numbers in this calculator reflect the latest IRS and state revenue department figures, but always verify with a tax professional before making major financial decisions.\"}]]}]\n42:[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm sm:text-base\",\"children\":\"Can I compare job offers with different benefits?\"}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"qrunsl\",{\"d\":\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes. You can adjust 401(k) contributions and HSA contributions for each scenario. If one job offers a 5% 401(k) match and another does not, enter the contribution amounts to see how pre-tax deductions affect your net take-home pay.\"}]]}]\n43:[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm sm:text-base\",\"children\":\"Is this calculator accurate for 2026?\"}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"qrunsl\",{\"d\":\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes. All federal tax brackets, standard deductions, FICA rates, and state tax rates are updated for the 2026 tax year. The 2026 Social Security wage base is $184,500, the standard deduction is $16,100 for single filers, and state rates reflect the latest published figures from each state revenue department.\"}]]}]\n33:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"c